    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50585" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰοειδής</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴον</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>like the flower</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1
				</span></i>
			, <i>purple</i>, in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always of the sea, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰοειδέα
			πόντον</span>, whether calm or stormy, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.298
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				5.56
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				11.107
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				844
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρήνη</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰός</span> B) <i>poisonous</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέντρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					886
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοιγός</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				243
			</span></i>. [<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
			</span></i> makes <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ</span> short, as
			conversely he has <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑάσι</span> from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴον</span> (q.v.).]</div>
